        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. 🇮🇩 A deadly train collision near Jakarta has left 15 people dead and 88 injured. Issued on: 28/04/2026 - 17:34 On Monday evening, a long-distance train slammed into a stationary commuter train that had stopped after striking a vehicle at an unmonitored level crossing. All 15 victims were women. 🗣️ \"I thought I was going to die. We were trapped, but thank God, I made it out. It feels like a dream,\" said survivor Sausan Sarifah. Indonesia's president has ordered an investigation and called for tighter safety measures at level crossings. Paris Saint-Germain vs Bayern Munich: Champions League semi-final showdown 28/04/2026 King Charles to promote British-American unity in speech to Congress 28/04/2026 Defending champion PSG faces 6-time winner Bayern in Champions League semifinal 28/04/2026 Hezbollah-Israel ceasefire under strain as both sides trade fire 28/04/2026 Colombia climate conference highlights lack of financing for shift from fossil fuels 28/04/2026 French public media in the dock: Report led by far right ally raises concerns 28/04/2026 Dozens of Gaza children arrive in Jordan for medical care 28/04/2026 Mali PM urges 'not to panic' after coordinated attack by jihadists, separatists 28/04/2026 King Charles in US for state visit amid differences over Iran war 28/04/2026"
